From 48567bc5f139f163826c1d19465a9476c23f3681 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:56:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 266/271] usb: typec: tcpci_mt6720: Add a driver for the
 MediaTek MT6720

The MT6720's port controller is TCPCI (VID 0x29cf, PID 0x6720, PD 3.0).
Initialise it as MediaTek's tcpc_mt6379 driver does for the MT6720: a
soft reset, the BMC PHY timings, the CC and VBUS filters, the I2C
timeout reset its GPIO interrupt needs, and auto idle with the fix that
keeps it from blocking transmission.

The reset leaves the reset-to-default fault set with every alert
unmasked, which raised the interrupt about 160 times a second until the
fault was cleared, so clear it and unmask only the alerts the TCPCI core
handles. The charger takes VBUS by itself, so sinking needs no command;
sourcing switches the optional vbus supply.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/Kconfig        |  11 +
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/Makefile       |   1 +
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci_mt6720.c | 342 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 354 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci_mt6720.c

